{"id":18630830909975,"type":"song","name":"Touch Me, I'm Sick","artist":"Mudhoney","year":1988,"weight":19,"info":{"yt":"_nGsT_qFMBs","cover":"https://lastfm-img.freetls.fastly.net/i/u/300x300/b673c7e172bb47c99fe20104a1c6518e.png"},"artist_ref":{"id":128392674410300,"name":"Mudhoney","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Mudhoney_June_2007.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[],"lists":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"Released in 1988, this track was Mudhoney's first single and is described as a quintessential example of grunge music. It had a local impact in Seattle and, in an alternate scenario, could have been the song that launched the entire grunge phenomenon globally. \"This was Mudhoney's first single. If this isn't Grunge, I don't know what it is. Mudhoney, and touch me, I'm sick from 1988.\"","year":1988,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"Peaked Too Soon - Bands That Were Ahead of Their Time","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Cy5SCQV0HAY"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":null,"body":"An early grunge classic, released in early 1988 by Mudhoney, characterized as rough, raw, and definitely uncommercial. This song was released by the independent label Sub Pop. \"That's mudhoney with an early grunge classic. Touch me I'm sick. From early 1988.\"","year":1988,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The 90s Part 3: Grunge","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tFBSrKMEZxI"}]}],"book_tracks":[{"id":18630830909975,"artist":"Mudhoney","artist_id":128392674410300,"title":"Touch Me I'm Sick","year":1988,"ess":0,"yt":"_nGsT_qFMBs","kind":"s","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Grunge","scene_id":32992220995517,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/#grunge","chapters":["Sección 5.15"],"pages":[[1,183,null]]}],"others":[{"id":